  "longBio": "Elliot Roth builds the infrastructure that lets more people do biology. He founded Spira, which biomanufactured genetically engineered algae into pigments and materials for BMW, Colgate, Clorox and Molson-Coors; co-founded Indie Lab RVA and the Biopunk Community, a network of 20+ laboratories and 5,000+ practitioners; and currently runs the Biopunk Fund and California Shine. Somewhere in there he built a robotic COVID testing lab inside a shipping container in two weeks, got legislation passed in Virginia, and ran a crowdfunded project on growing edible algae on the moon.",
